meta {
  name: 01 Get subscription
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/subscription
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq TRIAL_PENDING
  res.body.studentsMayLearn: eq false
}

docs {
  Run `Center Auth / 03 Login` first — this needs a live `accessToken`.

  A freshly registered center sits at TRIAL_PENDING with `studentsMayLearn`
  false. The trial clock starts at the first student activation (Phase 4), not
  at registration, so a center that never provisions anyone never burns its 30
  days. That is why this is the expected state and not TRIAL.

  Checks worth doing by hand:

  - no Authorization header  -> 401
  - a STUDENT access token   -> 401, the center verifier refuses it outright
  - after `Center Auth / 05 Logout` -> 401

  `status` is computed from the timestamps on every read, never stored. To see
  a different state, change `paid_until` directly in the database and re-run
  this request — no job has to run, and the answer changes immediately:

      paid_until = now + 5 days   -> ACTIVE,       studentsMayLearn true
      paid_until = now - 2 days   -> GRACE_PERIOD, studentsMayLearn true
      paid_until = now - 30 days  -> BLOCKED,      studentsMayLearn false

  `graceEndsAt` is null whenever `paid_until` is null. An expired trial gets no
  grace — it blocks the instant it ends.

  This endpoint must keep answering while BLOCKED. A blocked center still needs
  to see what it owes in order to pay it.
}
